---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Wordmark from "../components/Wordmark.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const lastUpdated = "2026-05-13";
---

<Layout title="Privacy — CustomerCue">
  <header class="flex items-center px-6 py-5 md:px-10">
    <a href="/" class="focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent focus-visible:ring-offset-2 focus-visible:ring-offset-background rounded-sm">
      <Wordmark />
    </a>
  </header>
  <main class="px-6 py-12 md:px-10 md:py-20">
    <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
      <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight md:text-4xl mb-8">
        Privacy
      </h1>

      <div class="space-y-6 text-base leading-relaxed text-foreground/90">
        <p class="font-display text-xl text-foreground">
          We don&rsquo;t set cookies. We don&rsquo;t track visitors. We don&rsquo;t run analytics.
        </p>

        <p>
          This marketing site is a lightweight introduction to CustomerCue. It loads
          HTML, CSS, a small amount of JavaScript, and web fonts from Google Fonts.
          We don&rsquo;t write to <code class="font-mono text-sm">localStorage</code> or
          <code class="font-mono text-sm">sessionStorage</code>.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight pt-4">
          What we don&rsquo;t collect
        </h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
          <li>No first- or third-party cookies.</li>
          <li>No <code class="font-mono text-sm">localStorage</code> or <code class="font-mono text-sm">sessionStorage</code>.</li>
          <li>No analytics SDKs (no Google Analytics, no Plausible, no PostHog, no Segment).</li>
          <li>No marketing pixels, attribution tags, or session replay.</li>
          <li>No fingerprinting.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight pt-4">
          What happens if you contact us
        </h2>
        <p>
          If you submit one of the forms on the homepage, your browser sends the
          form fields to our <code class="font-mono text-sm">/api/lead</code> endpoint.
          In this workshop demo, that endpoint validates the payload and returns a
          success response &mdash; it does not persist submissions. The conversations
          upload form does not upload the file itself (only its name, size, and type).
          You can also email us directly at <a href="mailto:hello@customercue.com" class="text-accent underline-offset-2 hover:underline">hello@customercue.com</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight pt-4">
          If this ever changes
        </h2>
        <p>
          If CustomerCue adds analytics, embedded video, scheduling widgets, or
          anything else that touches your browser&rsquo;s storage, we&rsquo;ll add a clear
          consent surface at the same time &mdash; not before. See
          <a href="https://github.com/phassle/CustomerCue/blob/main/docs/adr/0004-no-cookie-consent-banner.md" class="text-accent underline-offset-2 hover:underline">ADR&nbsp;0004</a>
          for the reasoning.
        </p>

        <p class="text-sm text-muted pt-8">
          Last updated {lastUpdated}.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
